{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba src/cljc/dao/stream/middleware.cljc'","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns dao.stream.middleware\n     2\t  \"DaoStream middleware: a handle-level adapter value, one `in` transform\n     3\t   over the operation map and one `out` transform over the outcome map\n     4\t   (docs/design/dao.stream.middleware.md).\n     5\t\n     6\t   A middleware is a value, never a callback: every transform here is\n     7\t   called downward by the caller and returns at once. `wrap` composes a\n     8\t   chain over a handle; `apply-request` is the one place an operation map\n     9\t   becomes a protocol call; `gate` and `present` are the two generic\n    10\t   middlewares; `encryption` and `metering` are the spec's exemplars;\n    11\t   `channel-allow-list` is the trivial policy this repository ships with.\n    12\t\n    13\t   The position rule and the four prohibitions are structural properties\n    14\t   of this design, not runtime checks: a transform is total, returns at\n    15\t   once, never loops, retries, waits or touches the inner handle, and\n    16\t   maps inner position p to outer position p for every p.\"\n    17\t  (:require [dao.stream :as stream]))\n    18\t\n    19\t\n    20\t;; =============================================================================\n    21\t;; The one dispatch point\n    22\t;; =============================================================================\n    23\t\n    24\t(defn- dispatch\n    25\t  \"Apply one operation map to a plain handle: the place an operation map\n    26\t   becomes a protocol call. An op outside the middleware vocabulary\n    27\t   (cursor, next, append!) is a defect in the host's own assembly -- the\n    28\t   mirror validates ops before this -- so it throws, per the contract's\n    29\t   reservation of exceptions (dao.stream.md, Result Convention).\"\n    30\t  [h req]\n    31\t  (let [[arg] (:dao.stream.remote/args req)]\n    32\t    (case (:dao.stream.remote/op req)\n    33\t      :dao.stream/cursor (stream/cursor h arg)\n    34\t      :dao.stream/next (stream/next h arg)\n    35\t      :dao.stream/append! (stream/append! h arg)\n    36\t      (throw (ex-info \"dao.stream.middleware: unknown operation\"\n    37\t                      {:op (:dao.stream.remote/op req)})))))\n    38\t\n    39\t\n    40\t(defprotocol IMiddlewareHandle\n    41\t  \"Internal seam of this namespace: the handle `wrap` returns answers one\n    42\t   whole chain pass under a caller-supplied context. `apply-request` uses\n    43\t   it so a composition (the mirror step of dao.stream.remote.md) can run\n    44\t   a table entry's middleware with its own context, exactly as the\n    45\t   wrapped handle's protocol methods run it with the local caller's {}.\n    46\t   Call `apply-request`, never this.\"\n    47\t\n    48\t  (operate-through\n    49\t    [handle ctx req]\n    50\t    \"Run the wrapped chain for operation map `req` under `ctx`.\"))\n    51\t\n    52\t\n    53\t(defn apply-request\n    54\t  \"Applies one operation map to a handle: `(apply-request h ctx req) ->\n    55\t   outcome`. On a plain handle this is the protocol call and `ctx` is\n    56\t   unused. On a handle `wrap` returned, this is the whole chain pass\n    57\t   under `ctx`: the entry point the mirror step composes with a channel\n    58\t   context. Extra qualified keys on `req` pass through untouched.\"\n    59\t  [h ctx req]\n    60\t  (if (satisfies? IMiddlewareHandle h)\n    61\t    (operate-through h ctx req)\n    62\t    (dispatch h req)))\n    63\t\n    64\t\n    65\t;; =============================================================================\n    66\t;; wrap\n    67\t;; =============================================================================\n    68\t\n    69\t(defn- run-outs\n    70\t  \"Run every `out` transform from the innermost outward over `outcome`,\n    71\t   for the middlewares at chain indices below `upto`.\"\n    72\t  [chain ctx req outcome upto]\n    73\t  (reduce\n    74\t    (fn [out i]\n    75\t      (let [middleware (nth chain i)]\n    76\t        ((:dao.stream.middleware/out middleware) ctx req out)))\n    77\t    outcome\n    78\t    (range (dec upto) -1 -1)))\n    79\t\n    80\t\n    81\t(defn- operate\n    82\t  \"One pass of `chain` over `req` under `ctx`: every `in` from the\n    83\t   outermost inward, the final request applied to `h` with\n    84\t   `apply-request` (which recurses into an inner wrapped handle, so\n    85\t   `ctx` carries through nesting), every `out` from the innermost\n    86\t   outward. An `in` answering an outcome map short-circuits: the inner\n    87\t   handle is not consulted and only the middlewares outside it\n    88\t   transform the outcome.\"\n    89\t  [h chain ctx req]\n    90\t  (loop [i 0, req req]\n    91\t    (if (= i (count chain))\n    92\t      (run-outs chain ctx req (apply-request h ctx req) (count chain))\n    93\t      (let [res ((:dao.stream.middleware/in (nth chain i)) ctx req)]\n    94\t        (if (stream/outcome-map? res)\n    95\t          (run-outs chain ctx req res i)\n    96\t          (recur (inc i) res))))))\n    97\t\n    98\t\n    99\t(defn wrap\n   100\t  \"Compose `chain`, a vector of middleware values applied outermost\n   101\t   first, over handle `h`. The returned handle implements exactly the\n   102\t   protocols `h` implements -- descriptor, which every handle carries,\n   103\t   plus its reader, writer and closable surfaces. On each protocol call\n   104\t   it builds the operation map, runs every `in` outermost inward,\n   105\t   applies the result to `h` with `apply-request` under the local\n   106\t   caller's {} context, and runs every `out` innermost outward.\n   107\t   `descriptor` and `close!` delegate to `h` unchanged: no middleware\n   108\t   sees them. The surface branches below are plain reify forms, one per\n   109\t   combination, because a handle implements its surface and no other.\"\n   110\t  [h chain]\n   111\t  (let [chain (vec chain)\n   112\t        flow (fn [ctx req] (operate h chain ctx req))\n   113\t        r? (stream/reader? h)\n   114\t        w? (stream/writer? h)\n   115\t        c? (stream/closable? h)]\n   116\t    (cond\n   117\t      (and r? w? c?)\n   118\t      (reify\n   119\t        IMiddlewareHandle\n   120\t        (operate-through [_ ctx req] (flow ctx req))\n   121\t\n   122\t\n   123\t        stream/IDaoStreamDescriptor\n   124\t\n   125\t        (descriptor [_] (stream/descriptor h))\n   126\t\n   127\t\n   128\t        stream/IDaoStreamReader\n   129\t\n   130\t        (cursor\n   131\t          [_ anchor]\n   132\t          (flow {} {:dao.stream.remote/op :dao.stream/cursor\n   133\t                    :dao.stream.remote/args [anchor]}))\n   134\t\n   135\t        (next\n   136\t          [_ c]\n   137\t          (flow {} {:dao.stream.remote/op :dao.stream/next\n   138\t                    :dao.stream.remote/args [c]}))\n   139\t\n   140\t\n   141\t        stream/IDaoStreamWriter\n   142\t\n   143\t        (append!\n   144\t          [_ v]\n   145\t          (flow {} {:dao.stream.remote/op :dao.stream/append!\n   146\t                    :dao.stream.remote/args [v]}))\n   147\t\n   148\t\n   149\t        stream/IDaoStreamClosable\n   150\t\n   151\t        (close! [_] (stream/close! h)))\n   152\t\n   153\t      (and r? w?)\n   154\t      (reify\n   155\t        IMiddlewareHandle\n   156\t        (operate-through [_ ctx req] (flow ctx req))\n   157\t\n   158\t\n   159\t        stream/IDaoStreamDescriptor\n   160\t\n   161\t        (descriptor [_] (stream/descriptor h))\n   162\t\n   163\t\n   164\t        stream/IDaoStreamReader\n   165\t\n   166\t        (cursor\n   167\t          [_ anchor]\n   168\t          (flow {} {:dao.stream.remote/op :dao.stream/cursor\n   169\t                    :dao.stream.remote/args [anchor]}))\n   170\t\n   171\t        (next\n   172\t          [_ c]\n   173\t          (flow {} {:dao.stream.remote/op :dao.stream/next\n   174\t                    :dao.stream.remote/args [c]}))\n   175\t\n   176\t\n   177\t        stream/IDaoStreamWriter\n   178\t\n   179\t        (append!\n   180\t          [_ v]\n   181\t          (flow {} {:dao.stream.remote/op :dao.stream/append!\n   182\t                    :dao.stream.remote/args [v]})))\n   183\t\n   184\t      (and r? c?)\n   185\t      (reify\n   186\t        IMiddlewareHandle\n   187\t        (operate-through [_ ctx req] (flow ctx req))\n   188\t\n   189\t\n   190\t        stream/IDaoStreamDescriptor\n   191\t\n   192\t        (descriptor [_] (stream/descriptor h))\n   193\t\n   194\t\n   195\t        stream/IDaoStreamReader\n   196\t\n   197\t        (cursor\n   198\t          [_ anchor]\n   199\t          (flow {} {:dao.stream.remote/op :dao.stream/cursor\n   200\t                    :dao.stream.remote/args [anchor]}))\n   201\t\n   202\t        (next\n   203\t          [_ c]\n   204\t          (flow {} {:dao.stream.remote/op :dao.stream/next\n   205\t                    :dao.stream.remote/args [c]}))\n   206\t\n   207\t\n   208\t        stream/IDaoStreamClosable\n   209\t\n   210\t        (close! [_] (stream/close! h)))\n   211\t\n   212\t      (and w? c?)\n   213\t      (reify\n   214\t        IMiddlewareHandle\n   215\t        (operate-through [_ ctx req] (flow ctx req))\n   216\t\n   217\t\n   218\t        stream/IDaoStreamDescriptor\n   219\t\n   220\t        (descriptor [_] (stream/descriptor h))\n   221\t\n   222\t\n   223\t        stream/IDaoStreamWriter\n   224\t\n   225\t        (append!\n   226\t          [_ v]\n   227\t          (flow {} {:dao.stream.remote/op :dao.stream/append!\n   228\t                    :dao.stream.remote/args [v]}))\n   229\t\n   230\t\n   231\t        stream/IDaoStreamClosable\n   232\t\n   233\t        (close! [_] (stream/close! h)))\n   234\t\n   235\t      r?\n   236\t      (reify\n   237\t        IMiddlewareHandle\n   238\t        (operate-through [_ ctx req] (flow ctx req))\n   239\t\n   240\t\n   241\t        stream/IDaoStreamDescriptor\n   242\t\n   243\t        (descriptor [_] (stream/descriptor h))\n   244\t\n   245\t\n   246\t        stream/IDaoStreamReader\n   247\t\n   248\t        (cursor\n   249\t          [_ anchor]\n   250\t          (flow {} {:dao.stream.remote/op :dao.stream/cursor\n   251\t                    :dao.stream.remote/args [anchor]}))\n   252\t\n   253\t        (next\n   254\t          [_ c]\n   255\t          (flow {} {:dao.stream.remote/op :dao.stream/next\n   256\t                    :dao.stream.remote/args [c]})))\n   257\t\n   258\t      w?\n   259\t      (reify\n   260\t        IMiddlewareHandle\n   261\t        (operate-through [_ ctx req] (flow ctx req))\n   262\t\n   263\t\n   264\t        stream/IDaoStreamDescriptor\n   265\t\n   266\t        (descriptor [_] (stream/descriptor h))\n   267\t\n   268\t\n   269\t        stream/IDaoStreamWriter\n   270\t\n   271\t        (append!\n   272\t          [_ v]\n   273\t          (flow {} {:dao.stream.remote/op :dao.stream/append!\n   274\t                    :dao.stream.remote/args [v]})))\n   275\t\n   276\t      c?\n   277\t      (reify\n   278\t        IMiddlewareHandle\n   279\t        (operate-through [_ ctx req] (flow ctx req))\n   280\t\n   281\t\n   282\t        stream/IDaoStreamDescriptor\n   283\t\n   284\t        (descriptor [_] (stream/descriptor h))\n   285\t\n   286\t\n   287\t        stream/IDaoStreamClosable\n   288\t\n   289\t        (close! [_] (stream/close! h)))\n   290\t\n   291\t      :else\n   292\t      (reify\n   293\t        IMiddlewareHandle\n   294\t        (operate-through [_ ctx req] (flow ctx req))\n   295\t\n   296\t\n   297\t        stream/IDaoStreamDescriptor\n   298\t\n   299\t        (descriptor [_] (stream/descriptor h))))))\n   300\t\n   301\t\n   302\t;; =============================================================================\n   303\t;; gate, the authorize step\n   304\t;; =============================================================================\n   305\t\n   306\t(def ^:private none-marker\n   307\t  \"The decision `verify` receives when the gate has none: no minted\n   308\t   cursor, no value observed yet, or a value cleared by a failed read.\n   309\t   A policy that must fail closed refuses it.\"\n   310\t  {:dao.stream.middleware/none true})\n   311\t\n   312\t\n   313\t(def ^:private ended-marker\n   314\t  \"The decision `verify` receives once the gate is ended: the medium\n   315\t   answered end, so no later operation reads it.\"\n   316\t  {:dao.stream.middleware/ended true})\n   317\t\n   318\t\n   319\t(defn gate\n   320\t  \"The authorize step: `(gate {:dao.stream.middleware/verify verify\n   321\t   :dao.stream.middleware/decision medium})` -> middleware. Mints its\n   322\t   read cursor with `cursor` :oldest on the decision medium once, at\n   323\t   construction. Each operation retries the mint once when it has no\n   324\t   cursor, then calls `next` on the medium once, plus the one recovery\n   325\t   re-read after a gap; when the medium answers end the gate becomes\n   326\t   ended and reads no more. `verify` is `(fn [decision ctx req] -> nil |\n   327\t   reason)`, the adapter contract of dao.shibi.md: nil passes the\n   328\t   request through; a reason short-circuits with :dao.stream/refused.\n   329\t   The cursor and last value are this middleware value's state, so use\n   330\t   one `gate` value per wrapped handle, and serialize calls on it.\"\n   331\t  [opts]\n   332\t  (let [verify (:dao.stream.middleware/verify opts)\n   333\t        decision (:dao.stream.middleware/decision opts)\n   334\t        state (volatile! {:cursor nil :value? false :value nil\n   335\t                          :ended? false})\n   336\t        mint!\n   337\t        (fn []\n   338\t          (let [r (stream/cursor decision stream/anchor-oldest)]\n   339\t            (when (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r))\n   340\t              (:dao.stream/cursor r))))\n   341\t\n   342\t        store! (fn [s] (vreset! state s) s)\n   343\t\n   344\t        absorb\n   345\t        (fn [s r]\n   346\t          (case (:dao.stream/outcome r)\n   347\t            :dao.stream/ok\n   348\t            {:cursor (:dao.stream/cursor r) :value? true\n   349\t             :value (:dao.stream/value r) :ended? false}\n   350\t\n   351\t            :dao.stream/blocked s\n   352\t\n   353\t            :dao.stream/end\n   354\t            {:cursor nil :value? false :value nil :ended? true}\n   355\t\n   356\t            :dao.stream/gap\n   357\t            ;; One recovery re-read; never a third read this operation.\n   358\t            (let [rec (:dao.stream/cursor r)\n   359\t                  r2 (stream/next decision rec)]\n   360\t              (case (:dao.stream/outcome r2)\n   361\t                :dao.stream/ok\n   362\t                {:cursor (:dao.stream/cursor r2) :value? true\n   363\t                 :value (:dao.stream/value r2) :ended? false}\n   364\t\n   365\t                :dao.stream/blocked\n   366\t                {:cursor rec :value? false :value nil :ended? false}\n   367\t\n   368\t                :dao.stream/end\n   369\t                {:cursor nil :value? false :value nil :ended? true}\n   370\t\n   371\t                {:cursor (get r2 :dao.stream/cursor) :value? false\n   372\t                 :value nil :ended? false}))\n   373\t\n   374\t            ;; Any other non-ok outcome clears value and cursor; the\n   375\t            ;; mint is retried afresh next operation.\n   376\t            {:cursor nil :value? false :value nil :ended? false}))\n   377\t\n   378\t        latest\n   379\t        (fn []\n   380\t          (let [s0 @state]\n   381\t            (if (:ended? s0)\n   382\t              ended-marker\n   383\t              (do\n   384\t                (when-not (:cursor s0)\n   385\t                  (when-let [c (mint!)]\n   386\t                    (store! (assoc s0 :cursor c))))\n   387\t                (let [s1 @state]\n   388\t                  (when (:cursor s1)\n   389\t                    (store! (absorb s1 (stream/next decision\n   390\t                                                    (:cursor s1)))))\n   391\t                  (let [s2 @state]\n   392\t                    (cond (:ended? s2) ended-marker\n   393\t                          (:value? s2) (:value s2)\n   394\t                          :else none-marker)))))))\n   395\t        _\n   396\t        (when-let [c (mint!)]\n   397\t          (store! (assoc @state :cursor c)))]\n   398\t    {:dao.stream.middleware/in\n   399\t     (fn [ctx req]\n   400\t       (let [reason (verify (latest) ctx req)]\n   401\t         (if (nil? reason)\n   402\t           req\n   403\t           {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/refused\n   404\t            :dao.stream.middleware/reason reason})))\n   405\t     :dao.stream.middleware/out\n   406\t     (fn [_ctx _req outcome] outcome)}))\n   407\t\n   408\t\n   409\t;; =============================================================================\n   410\t;; present, the credential step\n   411\t;; =============================================================================\n   412\t\n   413\t(defn present\n   414\t  \"The credential step: `(present {:dao.stream.middleware/present f})`\n   415\t   -> middleware, where `f` is `(fn [ctx req] -> credential)`. Its `in`\n   416\t   associates the result under :dao.stream.remote/credential on the\n   417\t   operation map; its `out` is identity.\"\n   418\t  [opts]\n   419\t  (let [present-fn (:dao.stream.middleware/present opts)]\n   420\t    {:dao.stream.middleware/in\n   421\t     (fn [ctx req]\n   422\t       (assoc req :dao.stream.remote/credential (present-fn ctx req)))\n   423\t     :dao.stream.middleware/out\n   424\t     (fn [_ctx _req outcome] outcome)}))\n   425\t\n   426\t\n   427\t;; =============================================================================\n   428\t;; Exemplars\n   429\t;; =============================================================================\n   430\t\n   431\t(defn encryption\n   432\t  \"The spec's value-encryption exemplar. `encipher` and `decipher` come\n   433\t   from a library cipher; the key is an argument to whatever built them.\n   434\t   `in` on append! replaces the value with its ciphertext, answering\n   435\t   :dao.stream/invalid-value when the value cannot be transformed on the\n   436\t   way in. `out` on an ok from next replaces :dao.stream/value with the\n   437\t   plaintext or, when it cannot be transformed on the way out, with\n   438\t   {:dao.stream.middleware/undecodable true :dao.stream.middleware/raw\n   439\t   v}, the outcome and cursor untouched. Cursors are never touched.\"\n   440\t  [opts]\n   441\t  (let [encipher (:dao.stream.middleware/encipher opts)\n   442\t        decipher (:dao.stream.middleware/decipher opts)]\n   443\t    {:dao.stream.middleware/in\n   444\t     (fn [_ctx req]\n   445\t       (if (= :dao.stream/append! (:dao.stream.remote/op req))\n   446\t         (try\n   447\t           (update-in req [:dao.stream.remote/args 0] encipher)\n   448\t           (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs js/Error) _\n   449\t             {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/invalid-value}))\n   450\t         req))\n   451\t     :dao.stream.middleware/out\n   452\t     (fn [_ctx req outcome]\n   453\t       (if (and (= :dao.stream/next (:dao.stream.remote/op req))\n   454\t                (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome outcome)))\n   455\t         (try\n   456\t           (update outcome :dao.stream/value decipher)\n   457\t           (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs js/Error) _\n   458\t             (assoc outcome :dao.stream/value\n   459\t                    {:dao.stream.middleware/undecodable true\n   460\t                     :dao.stream.middleware/raw\n   461\t                     (:dao.stream/value outcome)})))\n   462\t         outcome))}))\n   463\t\n   464\t\n   465\t(defn metering\n   466\t  \"The spec's metering exemplar: `out` appends {:meter/identity id\n   467\t   :meter/op op :meter/outcome kind} to the composed metering stream\n   468\t   `sink` and returns the outcome unchanged. The side effect is a\n   469\t   stream emission, never a retry or a wait.\"\n   470\t  [opts]\n   471\t  (let [sink (:meter/stream opts)\n   472\t        id (:meter/identity opts)]\n   473\t    {:dao.stream.middleware/in\n   474\t     (fn [_ctx req] req)\n   475\t     :dao.stream.middleware/out\n   476\t     (fn [_ctx req outcome]\n   477\t       (stream/append! sink\n   478\t                       {:meter/identity id\n   479\t                        :meter/op (:dao.stream.remote/op req)\n   480\t                        :meter/outcome (:dao.stream/outcome outcome)})\n   481\t       outcome)}))\n   482\t\n   483\t\n   484\t;; =============================================================================\n   485\t;; The trivial policy this repository ships with\n   486\t;; =============================================================================\n   487\t\n   488\t(defn channel-allow-list\n   489\t  \"An allow-list `verify` for `gate`, keyed on\n   490\t   :dao.stream.remote/channel in ctx and ignoring the credential and the\n   491\t   decision: nil for a channel identity in `allowed`, a refusal reason\n   492\t   for anything else, a missing channel included. The reason vocabulary\n   493\t   itself belongs to dao.shibi.md; this one is composition-owned.\"\n   494\t  [allowed]\n   495\t  (fn [_decision ctx _req]\n   496\t    (if (contains? allowed (:dao.stream.remote/channel ctx))\n   497\t      nil\n   498\t      :dao.stream.middleware/channel-not-allowed)))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
