{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba test/dao/stream/middleware_test.cljc'","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns dao.stream.middleware-test\n     2\t  \"The middleware slice: the position rule under a value cipher over a\n     3\t   ring buffer; the allow-list gate refusing with :dao.stream/refused; a\n     4\t   gate reading the latest decision through a capacity-1 medium after\n     5\t   eviction; a filter that cannot be expressed; and the operation rules\n     6\t   of apply-request and wrap, the short-circuit ordering, the failure\n     7\t   markers, the gate's decision-read lifecycle, metering and present.\"\n     8\t  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n     9\t            [dao.stream :as stream]\n    10\t            [dao.stream.middleware :as mw]\n    11\t            [dao.stream.ringbuffer :as ringbuffer]))\n    12\t\n    13\t\n    14\t;; =============================================================================\n    15\t;; Test support\n    16\t;; =============================================================================\n    17\t\n    18\t(defn- ring\n    19\t  \"An open owner ring-buffer handle with the given capacity.\"\n    20\t  [capacity]\n    21\t  (:dao.stream/handle\n    22\t    (ringbuffer/create! {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream/ringbuffer\n    23\t                         :dao.stream.ringbuffer/capacity capacity})))\n    24\t\n    25\t\n    26\t(defn- drain-values\n    27\t  \"Every retained value of `h`, oldest first, by a fresh cursor walk.\"\n    28\t  [h]\n    29\t  (loop [c (:dao.stream/cursor (stream/cursor h :dao.stream/oldest))\n    30\t         acc []]\n    31\t    (let [r (stream/next h c)]\n    32\t      (if (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r))\n    33\t        (recur (:dao.stream/cursor r) (conj acc (:dao.stream/value r)))\n    34\t        acc))))\n    35\t\n    36\t\n    37\t(defn- encipher\n    38\t  \"The test cipher's encipher half: a tagged map, total and invertible.\"\n    39\t  [v]\n    40\t  {:cipher/of v})\n    41\t\n    42\t\n    43\t(defn- decipher\n    44\t  \"The test cipher's decipher half: it throws on anything that is not\n    45\t   its own ciphertext, as a library cipher fails on a corrupt value.\"\n    46\t  [v]\n    47\t  (if (and (map? v) (contains? v :cipher/of))\n    48\t    (:cipher/of v)\n    49\t    (throw (ex-info \"undecipherable\" {:value v}))))\n    50\t\n    51\t\n    52\t(defn- encryption\n    53\t  \"The spec's value-encryption exemplar over the test cipher.\"\n    54\t  []\n    55\t  (mw/encryption {:dao.stream.middleware/encipher encipher\n    56\t                  :dao.stream.middleware/decipher decipher}))\n    57\t\n    58\t\n    59\t(defn- recording-handle\n    60\t  \"A reader, writer and closable handle recording every protocol call in\n    61\t   `calls` and answering fixed contract-valid outcomes.\"\n    62\t  [calls]\n    63\t  (reify\n    64\t    stream/IDaoStreamDescriptor\n    65\t    (descriptor\n    66\t      [_]\n    67\t      (swap! calls conj :descriptor)\n    68\t      {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n    69\t       :dao.stream/descriptor {:dao.stream/type :test/only\n    70\t                               :dao.stream/identity :inner}\n    71\t       :dao.stream/identity :inner})\n    72\t\n    73\t\n    74\t    stream/IDaoStreamReader\n    75\t\n    76\t    (cursor\n    77\t      [_ anchor]\n    78\t      (swap! calls conj [:cursor anchor])\n    79\t      {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok :dao.stream/cursor :minted})\n    80\t\n    81\t    (next\n    82\t      [_ c]\n    83\t      (swap! calls conj [:next c])\n    84\t      {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n    85\t       :dao.stream/value :inner-value\n    86\t       :dao.stream/cursor :successor})\n    87\t\n    88\t\n    89\t    stream/IDaoStreamWriter\n    90\t\n    91\t    (append!\n    92\t      [_ v]\n    93\t      (swap! calls conj [:append! v])\n    94\t      {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok})\n    95\t\n    96\t\n    97\t    stream/IDaoStreamClosable\n    98\t\n    99\t    (close!\n   100\t      [_]\n   101\t      (swap! calls conj :close!)\n   102\t      {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok})))\n   103\t\n   104\t\n   105\t(defn- spy\n   106\t  \"A middleware recording [:in name] / [:out name] in `log` around the\n   107\t   given transform behavior.\"\n   108\t  [name log in-fn out-fn]\n   109\t  {:dao.stream.middleware/in\n   110\t   (fn [ctx req] (swap! log conj [:in name]) (in-fn ctx req))\n   111\t   :dao.stream.middleware/out\n   112\t   (fn [ctx req outcome]\n   113\t     (swap! log conj [:out name])\n   114\t     (out-fn ctx req outcome))})\n   115\t\n   116\t\n   117\t(defn- pass-in\n   118\t  [_ctx req]\n   119\t  req)\n   120\t\n   121\t\n   122\t(defn- pass-out\n   123\t  [_ctx _req outcome]\n   124\t  outcome)\n   125\t\n   126\t\n   127\t(defn- refuse-in\n   128\t  \"An `in` that short-circuits with a refused outcome naming `reason`.\"\n   129\t  [reason]\n   130\t  (fn [_ctx _req]\n   131\t    {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/refused\n   132\t     :dao.stream.middleware/reason reason}))\n   133\t\n   134\t\n   135\t(defn- scripted-medium\n   136\t  \"A reader-only decision medium: each `cursor` and `next` call is\n   137\t   recorded in `calls` and answered by popping the head of the matching\n   138\t   queue atom.\"\n   139\t  [calls cursors reads]\n   140\t  (reify\n   141\t    stream/IDaoStreamReader\n   142\t    (cursor\n   143\t      [_ anchor]\n   144\t      (swap! calls conj [:cursor anchor])\n   145\t      (let [[r & more] @cursors]\n   146\t        (reset! cursors more)\n   147\t        r))\n   148\t\n   149\t    (next\n   150\t      [_ c]\n   151\t      (swap! calls conj [:next c])\n   152\t      (let [[r & more] @reads]\n   153\t        (reset! reads more)\n   154\t        r))))\n   155\t\n   156\t\n   157\t(defn- ok-cursor\n   158\t  \"A scripted :ok cursor answer for `c`.\"\n   159\t  [c]\n   160\t  {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok :dao.stream/cursor c})\n   161\t\n   162\t\n   163\t(defn- ok-read\n   164\t  \"A scripted :ok read answer of `v` with successor cursor `c`.\"\n   165\t  [v c]\n   166\t  {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n   167\t   :dao.stream/value v :dao.stream/cursor c})\n   168\t\n   169\t\n   170\t(defn- gap-read\n   171\t  \"A scripted :gap read answer with recovery cursor `c`.\"\n   172\t  [c]\n   173\t  {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/gap :dao.stream/cursor c})\n   174\t\n   175\t\n   176\t;; =============================================================================\n   177\t;; apply-request\n   178\t;; =============================================================================\n   179\t\n   180\t(deftest apply-request-dispatches-each-operation-once\n   181\t  (let [h (ring 4)\n   182\t        c (:dao.stream/cursor\n   183\t            (mw/apply-request h {}\n   184\t                              {:dao.stream.remote/op :dao.stream/cursor\n   185\t                               :dao.stream.remote/args\n   186\t                               [:dao.stream/oldest]}))\n   187\t        a (mw/apply-request h {}\n   188\t                            {:dao.stream.remote/op :dao.stream/append!\n   189\t                             :dao.stream.remote/args [:v]\n   190\t                             :dao.stream.test/open :kept})\n   191\t        n (mw/apply-request h {}\n   192\t                            {:dao.stream.remote/op :dao.stream/next\n   193\t                             :dao.stream.remote/args [c]})]\n   194\t    (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome a)))\n   195\t    (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome n)))\n   196\t    (is (= :v (:dao.stream/value n)))\n   197\t    (is (= (stream/next h c) n) \"the protocol call itself, verbatim\")\n   198\t    (testing \"an op outside the middleware vocabulary is a host assembly\n   199\t              defect and throws\"\n   200\t      (is (thrown? #?(:clj Exception :cljs js/Error :cljd Object)\n   201\t            (mw/apply-request h {}\n   202\t                              {:dao.stream.remote/op\n   203\t                               :dao.stream/close!\n   204\t                               :dao.stream.remote/args []}))))))\n   205\t\n   206\t\n   207\t;; =============================================================================\n   208\t;; wrap: order, short-circuit, delegation, surfaces\n   209\t;; =============================================================================\n   210\t\n   211\t(deftest wrap-runs-ins-outermost-first-and-outs-innermost-outward\n   212\t  (let [calls (atom [])\n   213\t        log (atom [])\n   214\t        wrapped (mw/wrap (recording-handle calls)\n   215\t                         [(spy :a log pass-in pass-out)\n   216\t                          (spy :b log pass-in pass-out)])]\n   217\t    (is (= :dao.stream/ok\n   218\t           (:dao.stream/outcome (stream/append! wrapped :v))))\n   219\t    (is (= [[:in :a] [:in :b] [:out :b] [:out :a]] @log))\n   220\t    (is (= [[:append! :v]] @calls))))\n   221\t\n   222\t\n   223\t(deftest an-in-outcome-short-circuits-past-the-inner-handle\n   224\t  (let [calls (atom [])\n   225\t        log (atom [])\n   226\t        wrapped (mw/wrap (recording-handle calls)\n   227\t                         [(spy :a log pass-in pass-out)\n   228\t                          (spy :b log (refuse-in :b) pass-out)\n   229\t                          (spy :c log pass-in pass-out)])\n   230\t        outcome (stream/cursor wrapped :dao.stream/oldest)]\n   231\t    (is (= :dao.stream/refused (:dao.stream/outcome outcome)))\n   232\t    (is (= :b (:dao.stream.middleware/reason outcome)))\n   233\t    (is (= [] @calls) \"the inner handle is not consulted\")\n   234\t    (is (= [[:in :a] [:in :b] [:out :a]] @log)\n   235\t        \"only the middlewares outside b run their out transforms\")))\n   236\t\n   237\t\n   238\t(deftest descriptor-and-close-delegate-unchanged\n   239\t  (let [calls (atom [])\n   240\t        log (atom [])\n   241\t        h (recording-handle calls)\n   242\t        wrapped (mw/wrap h [(spy :a log pass-in pass-out)])]\n   243\t    (is (= (stream/descriptor h) (stream/descriptor wrapped)))\n   244\t    (is (= :dao.stream/ok\n   245\t           (:dao.stream/outcome (stream/close! wrapped))))\n   246\t    (is (= [:descriptor :descriptor :close!] @calls))\n   247\t    (is (empty? @log) \"no middleware sees descriptor or close!\")))\n   248\t\n   249\t\n   250\t(deftest the-wrapped-handle-implements-exactly-the-inner-surfaces\n   251\t  (let [reader-only\n   252\t        (reify stream/IDaoStreamReader\n   253\t          (cursor\n   254\t            [_ _]\n   255\t            {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n   256\t             :dao.stream/cursor :c})\n   257\t\n   258\t          (next [_ _] {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/blocked}))]\n   259\t    (let [w (mw/wrap reader-only\n   260\t                     [(spy :a (atom []) pass-in pass-out)])]\n   261\t      (is (stream/descriptor? w))\n   262\t      (is (stream/reader? w))\n   263\t      (is (not (stream/writer? w)))\n   264\t      (is (not (stream/closable? w))))\n   265\t    (let [w (mw/wrap (ring 2)\n   266\t                     [(spy :a (atom []) pass-in pass-out)])]\n   267\t      (is (stream/reader? w))\n   268\t      (is (stream/writer? w))\n   269\t      (is (stream/closable? w)))))\n   270\t\n   271\t\n   272\t;; =============================================================================\n   273\t;; The position rule under a value cipher over a ring buffer\n   274\t;; =============================================================================\n   275\t\n   276\t(deftest a-value-cipher-preserves-positions-cursors-and-outcomes\n   277\t  (let [inner (ring 4)\n   278\t        wrapped (mw/wrap inner [(encryption)])]\n   279\t    (is (= :dao.stream/ok\n   280\t           (:dao.stream/outcome (stream/append! wrapped :v1))))\n   281\t    (is (= :dao.stream/ok\n   282\t           (:dao.stream/outcome (stream/append! wrapped :v2))))\n   283\t    (is (= [{:cipher/of :v1} {:cipher/of :v2}] (drain-values inner))\n   284\t        \"the inner handle stores only ciphertext\")\n   285\t    (let [cw (:dao.stream/cursor\n   286\t               (stream/cursor wrapped :dao.stream/oldest))\n   287\t          ci (:dao.stream/cursor (stream/cursor inner :dao.stream/oldest))]\n   288\t      (is (= ci cw) \"the wrapped handle mints the inner handle's cursors\")\n   289\t      (let [rw (stream/next wrapped cw)\n   290\t            ri (stream/next inner ci)]\n   291\t        (is (= :v1 (:dao.stream/value rw))\n   292\t            \"the wrapped handle presents the plaintext\")\n   293\t        (is (= {:cipher/of :v1} (:dao.stream/value ri)))\n   294\t        (is (= (:dao.stream/cursor ri) (:dao.stream/cursor rw))\n   295\t            \"the successor cursor is the inner handle's own\")\n   296\t        (is (= (:dao.stream/outcome ri) (:dao.stream/outcome rw))\n   297\t            \"the outcome kind is untouched\"))))\n   298\t  (testing \"a gap crosses with the source's own recovery cursor\"\n   299\t    (let [inner (ring 2)\n   300\t          wrapped (mw/wrap inner [(encryption)])\n   301\t          ci (:dao.stream/cursor (stream/cursor inner :dao.stream/oldest))\n   302\t          cw (:dao.stream/cursor\n   303\t               (stream/cursor wrapped :dao.stream/oldest))]\n   304\t      (is (= ci cw))\n   305\t      (doseq [v [:v1 :v2 :v3]]\n   306\t        (is (= :dao.stream/ok\n   307\t               (:dao.stream/outcome (stream/append! wrapped v)))))\n   308\t      (let [gi (stream/next inner ci)\n   309\t            gw (stream/next wrapped cw)]\n   310\t        (is (= :dao.stream/gap (:dao.stream/outcome gw)))\n   311\t        (is (= (:dao.stream/cursor gi) (:dao.stream/cursor gw))\n   312\t            \"the recovery cursor is the source's, unparsed and unrewritten\")\n   313\t        (let [rw (stream/next wrapped (:dao.stream/cursor gw))]\n   314\t          (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome rw)))\n   315\t          (is (= :v2 (:dao.stream/value rw))\n   316\t              \"the recovery read presents the retained plaintext\")\n   317\t          (is (= :v3 (:dao.stream/value\n   318\t                       (stream/next wrapped (:dao.stream/cursor rw))))\n   319\t              \"and the walk continues to the newest plaintext\"))))))\n   320\t\n   321\t\n   322\t(deftest an-undecodable-value-is-presented-as-the-marker\n   323\t  (let [inner (ring 4)\n   324\t        wrapped (mw/wrap inner [(encryption)])]\n   325\t    (is (= :dao.stream/ok\n   326\t           (:dao.stream/outcome (stream/append! inner :raw))))\n   327\t    (let [c (:dao.stream/cursor\n   328\t              (stream/cursor wrapped :dao.stream/oldest))\n   329\t          plain (stream/next inner c)\n   330\t          r (stream/next wrapped c)]\n   331\t      (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r)))\n   332\t      (is (= {:dao.stream.middleware/undecodable true\n   333\t              :dao.stream.middleware/raw :raw}\n   334\t             (:dao.stream/value r)))\n   335\t      (is (= (:dao.stream/cursor plain) (:dao.stream/cursor r))\n   336\t          \"the cursor is untouched: the position is real\")\n   337\t      (is (= (:dao.stream/outcome plain) (:dao.stream/outcome r))\n   338\t          \"the outcome is untouched: the reader decides\"))))\n   339\t\n   340\t\n   341\t(deftest an-untransformable-value-answers-invalid-value-on-the-way-in\n   342\t  (let [inner (ring 4)\n   343\t        encipher (fn [v]\n   344\t                   (if (= v :poison)\n   345\t                     (throw (ex-info \"cannot encode\" {:value v}))\n   346\t                     {:cipher/of v}))\n   347\t        wrapped (mw/wrap inner\n   348\t                         [(mw/encryption\n   349\t                            {:dao.stream.middleware/encipher encipher\n   350\t                             :dao.stream.middleware/decipher decipher})])]\n   351\t    (is (= :dao.stream/invalid-value\n   352\t           (:dao.stream/outcome (stream/append! wrapped :poison))))\n   353\t    (is (empty? (drain-values inner))\n   354\t        \"nothing reached the inner handle and nothing was appended\")))\n   355\t\n   356\t\n   357\t;; =============================================================================\n   358\t;; A filter cannot be expressed\n   359\t;; =============================================================================\n   360\t\n   361\t(deftest a-filter-cannot-be-expressed\n   362\t  (testing \"an out may replace a value, never remove the position\"\n   363\t    (let [inner (ring 4)\n   364\t          tombstone\n   365\t          (spy :filter (atom []) pass-in\n   366\t               (fn [_ctx _req outcome]\n   367\t                 (if (and (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome outcome))\n   368\t                          (= :drop (:dao.stream/value outcome)))\n   369\t                   (assoc outcome :dao.stream/value :dropped)\n   370\t                   outcome)))\n   371\t          wrapped (mw/wrap inner [tombstone])]\n   372\t      (doseq [v [:a :drop :c]]\n   373\t        (is (= :dao.stream/ok\n   374\t               (:dao.stream/outcome (stream/append! wrapped v)))))\n   375\t      (loop [cw (:dao.stream/cursor\n   376\t                  (stream/cursor wrapped :dao.stream/oldest))\n   377\t             ci (:dao.stream/cursor\n   378\t                  (stream/cursor inner :dao.stream/oldest))\n   379\t             seen []]\n   380\t        (let [rw (stream/next wrapped cw)\n   381\t              ri (stream/next inner ci)]\n   382\t          (if (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome rw))\n   383\t            (do (is (= (:dao.stream/cursor ri) (:dao.stream/cursor rw))\n   384\t                    \"the chain keeps the inner handle's positions\")\n   385\t                (recur (:dao.stream/cursor rw) (:dao.stream/cursor ri)\n   386\t                       (conj seen (:dao.stream/value rw))))\n   387\t            (is (= [:a :dropped :c] seen)\n   388\t                \"every element is still presented: dropping is not a\n   389\t                 transform's to decide\"))))))\n   390\t  (testing \"declining one element declines the whole operation\"\n   391\t    (let [inner (ring 4)\n   392\t          wrapped (mw/wrap inner\n   393\t                           [(spy :gate (atom []) (refuse-in :filtered)\n   394\t                                 pass-out)])]\n   395\t      (is (= :dao.stream/refused\n   396\t             (:dao.stream/outcome (stream/append! wrapped :drop))))\n   397\t      (is (empty? (drain-values inner))\n   398\t          \"the stream holds nothing: a refusal is data, not a silent\n   399\t           skip\"))))\n   400\t\n   401\t\n   402\t;; =============================================================================\n   403\t;; gate\n   404\t;; =============================================================================\n   405\t\n   406\t(deftest a-gate-with-the-channel-allow-list-refuses\n   407\t  (let [inner (ring 4)\n   408\t        wrapped (mw/wrap inner\n   409\t                         [(mw/gate\n   410\t                            {:dao.stream.middleware/verify\n   411\t                             (mw/channel-allow-list #{\"a\"})\n   412\t                             :dao.stream.middleware/decision (ring 1)})])]\n   413\t    (testing \"a channel on the list passes and the operation lands\"\n   414\t      (is (= :dao.stream/ok\n   415\t             (:dao.stream/outcome\n   416\t               (mw/apply-request wrapped\n   417\t                                 {:dao.stream.remote/channel \"a\"}\n   418\t                                 {:dao.stream.remote/op :dao.stream/append!\n   419\t                                  :dao.stream.remote/args [:v]}))))\n   420\t      (is (= [:v] (drain-values inner))))\n   421\t    (testing \"a channel off the list is refused with its reason\"\n   422\t      (let [r (mw/apply-request wrapped\n   423\t                                {:dao.stream.remote/channel \"z\"}\n   424\t                                {:dao.stream.remote/op :dao.stream/append!\n   425\t                                 :dao.stream.remote/args [:w]})]\n   426\t        (is (= :dao.stream/refused (:dao.stream/outcome r)))\n   427\t        (is (= :dao.stream.middleware/channel-not-allowed\n   428\t               (:dao.stream.middleware/reason r))))\n   429\t      (is (= [:v] (drain-values inner)) \"nothing was appended\"))\n   430\t    (testing \"a local caller's {} context names no channel and refuses\"\n   431\t      (is (= :dao.stream/refused\n   432\t             (:dao.stream/outcome (stream/append! wrapped :x)))))))\n   433\t\n   434\t\n   435\t(deftest a-gate-reads-the-latest-decision-through-a-capacity-1-medium\n   436\t  (let [medium (ring 1)\n   437\t        seen (atom [])\n   438\t        gate-mw (mw/gate\n   439\t                  {:dao.stream.middleware/verify\n   440\t                   (fn [d _ctx _req] (swap! seen conj d) nil)\n   441\t                   :dao.stream.middleware/decision medium})\n   442\t        target (ring 4)\n   443\t        wrapped (mw/wrap target [gate-mw])\n   444\t        ;; One operation per gate pass: the cursor is the target's own,\n   445\t        ;; minted once, and every read! is one next through the gate.\n   446\t        c0 (:dao.stream/cursor (stream/cursor target :dao.stream/oldest))\n   447\t        read! (fn []\n   448\t                (mw/apply-request wrapped {}\n   449\t                                  {:dao.stream.remote/op :dao.stream/next\n   450\t                                   :dao.stream.remote/args [c0]}))]\n   451\t    (is (= :dao.stream/blocked (:dao.stream/outcome (read!))))\n   452\t    (is (= [{:dao.stream.middleware/none true}] @seen)\n   453\t        \"the medium has published nothing yet\")\n   454\t    (stream/append! medium :d1)\n   455\t    (read!)\n   456\t    (is (= [{:dao.stream.middleware/none true} :d1] @seen))\n   457\t    ;; Two further decisions evict :d1; the gate's cursor spans the\n   458\t    ;; eviction of :d2 as well.\n   459\t    (stream/append! medium :d2)\n   460\t    (stream/append! medium :d3)\n   461\t    (read!)\n   462\t    (is (= [{:dao.stream.middleware/none true} :d1 :d3] @seen)\n   463\t        \"the latest decision, recovered through the eviction\")))\n   464\t\n   465\t\n   466\t(deftest the-gate-decision-read-lifecycle\n   467\t  (testing \"the mint happens once, at gate construction\"\n   468\t    (let [calls (atom [])]\n   469\t      (mw/gate {:dao.stream.middleware/verify (fn [_ _ _] nil)\n   470\t                :dao.stream.middleware/decision\n   471\t                (scripted-medium calls (atom [(ok-cursor :c0)]) (atom []))})\n   472\t      (is (= [[:cursor :dao.stream/oldest]] @calls))))\n   473\t  (testing \"a mint that never answers ok leaves verify the none marker\"\n   474\t    (let [calls (atom [])\n   475\t          medium (scripted-medium\n   476\t                   calls\n   477\t                   (atom [{:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/transport-error}\n   478\t                          {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/transport-error}])\n   479\t                   (atom []))\n   480\t          seen (atom [])\n   481\t          gate-mw (mw/gate\n   482\t                    {:dao.stream.middleware/verify\n   483\t                     (fn [d _ctx _req] (swap! seen conj d) nil)\n   484\t                     :dao.stream.middleware/decision medium})\n   485\t          inner-calls (atom [])\n   486\t          wrapped (mw/wrap (recording-handle inner-calls) [gate-mw])]\n   487\t      (is (= :dao.stream/ok\n   488\t             (:dao.stream/outcome (stream/next wrapped :my-c))))\n   489\t      (is (= [{:dao.stream.middleware/none true}] @seen))\n   490\t      (is (= [[:cursor :dao.stream/oldest] [:cursor :dao.stream/oldest]] @calls)\n   491\t          \"the construction mint, then one retry this operation; next is\n   492\t           skipped\")\n   493\t      (is (= [[:next :my-c]] @inner-calls)\n   494\t          \"the request itself passes through unchanged\")))\n   495\t  (testing \"blocked keeps the cursor and the last value\"\n   496\t    (let [calls (atom [])\n   497\t          medium (scripted-medium calls\n   498\t                                  (atom [(ok-cursor :c0)])\n   499\t                                  (atom [(ok-read :d1 :c1)\n   500\t                                         {:dao.stream/outcome\n   501\t                                          :dao.stream/blocked}]))\n   502\t          seen (atom [])\n   503\t          wrapped (mw/wrap (ring 4)\n   504\t                           [(mw/gate\n   505\t                              {:dao.stream.middleware/verify\n   506\t                               (fn [d _ctx _req] (swap! seen conj d) nil)\n   507\t                               :dao.stream.middleware/decision medium})])]\n   508\t      (stream/next wrapped :c)\n   509\t      (stream/next wrapped :c)\n   510\t      (is (= [:d1 :d1] @seen) \"the last value is kept across blocked\")\n   511\t      (is (= [[:cursor :dao.stream/oldest] [:next :c0] [:next :c1]] @calls)\n   512\t          \"next is called once per operation\")))\n   513\t  (testing \"end ends the gate: no later operation reads the medium\"\n   514\t    (let [calls (atom [])\n   515\t          medium (scripted-medium calls\n   516\t                                  (atom [(ok-cursor :c0)])\n   517\t                                  (atom [{:dao.stream/outcome\n   518\t                                          :dao.stream/end}]))\n   519\t          seen (atom [])\n   520\t          wrapped (mw/wrap (ring 4)\n   521\t                           [(mw/gate\n   522\t                              {:dao.stream.middleware/verify\n   523\t                               (fn [d _ctx _req] (swap! seen conj d) nil)\n   524\t                               :dao.stream.middleware/decision medium})])]\n   525\t      (stream/next wrapped :c)\n   526\t      (stream/next wrapped :c)\n   527\t      (is (= [{:dao.stream.middleware/ended true}\n   528\t              {:dao.stream.middleware/ended true}] @seen))\n   529\t      (is (= [[:cursor :dao.stream/oldest] [:next :c0]] @calls)\n   530\t          \"the ended gate reads no more\")))\n   531\t  (testing \"one recovery read after a gap, then the latest value\"\n   532\t    (let [calls (atom [])\n   533\t          medium (scripted-medium calls\n   534\t                                  (atom [(ok-cursor :c0)])\n   535\t                                  (atom [(gap-read :c9)\n   536\t                                         (ok-read :d2 :c10)\n   537\t                                         {:dao.stream/outcome\n   538\t                                          :dao.stream/blocked}]))\n   539\t          seen (atom [])\n   540\t          wrapped (mw/wrap (ring 4)\n   541\t                           [(mw/gate\n   542\t                              {:dao.stream.middleware/verify\n   543\t                               (fn [d _ctx _req] (swap! seen conj d) nil)\n   544\t                               :dao.stream.middleware/decision medium})])]\n   545\t      (stream/next wrapped :c)\n   546\t      (stream/next wrapped :c)\n   547\t      (is (= [:d2 :d2] @seen))\n   548\t      (is (= [[:cursor :dao.stream/oldest] [:next :c0] [:next :c9] [:next :c10]]\n   549\t             @calls)\n   550\t          \"the gap adopts the recovery cursor and reads it once\")))\n   551\t  (testing \"a gap recovered by a gap stays without a value, no third read\"\n   552\t    (let [calls (atom [])\n   553\t          medium (scripted-medium calls\n   554\t                                  (atom [(ok-cursor :c0)])\n   555\t                                  (atom [(gap-read :c9)\n   556\t                                         (gap-read :c11)\n   557\t                                         {:dao.stream/outcome\n   558\t                                          :dao.stream/blocked}]))\n   559\t          seen (atom [])\n   560\t          wrapped (mw/wrap (ring 4)\n   561\t                           [(mw/gate\n   562\t                              {:dao.stream.middleware/verify\n   563\t                               (fn [d _ctx _req] (swap! seen conj d) nil)\n   564\t                               :dao.stream.middleware/decision medium})])]\n   565\t      (stream/next wrapped :c)\n   566\t      (stream/next wrapped :c)\n   567\t      (is (= [{:dao.stream.middleware/none true}\n   568\t              {:dao.stream.middleware/none true}] @seen))\n   569\t      (is (= [[:cursor :dao.stream/oldest] [:next :c0] [:next :c9] [:next :c11]]\n   570\t             @calls)\n   571\t          \"the second recovery cursor is adopted, never read twice\")))\n   572\t  (testing \"a non-ok read clears cursor and value; the mint retries afresh\"\n   573\t    (let [calls (atom [])\n   574\t          medium (scripted-medium\n   575\t                   calls\n   576\t                   (atom [(ok-cursor :c0) (ok-cursor :c1)])\n   577\t                   (atom [{:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/cursor-mismatch}\n   578\t                          (ok-read :d3 :c2)]))\n   579\t          seen (atom [])\n   580\t          wrapped (mw/wrap (ring 4)\n   581\t                           [(mw/gate\n   582\t                              {:dao.stream.middleware/verify\n   583\t                               (fn [d _ctx _req] (swap! seen conj d) nil)\n   584\t                               :dao.stream.middleware/decision medium})])]\n   585\t      (stream/next wrapped :c)\n   586\t      (stream/next wrapped :c)\n   587\t      (is (= [{:dao.stream.middleware/none true} :d3] @seen))\n   588\t      (is (= [[:cursor :dao.stream/oldest] [:next :c0]\n   589\t              [:cursor :dao.stream/oldest] [:next :c1]]\n   590\t             @calls)\n   591\t          \"the next operation mints afresh\")))\n   592\t  (testing \"nil passes the request through; a reason short-circuits\"\n   593\t    (let [calls (atom [])\n   594\t          inner-calls (atom [])\n   595\t          medium (scripted-medium\n   596\t                   calls\n   597\t                   (atom [(ok-cursor :c0)])\n   598\t                   (atom [(ok-read :good :c1) (ok-read :bad :c2)]))\n   599\t          wrapped (mw/wrap\n   600\t                    (recording-handle inner-calls)\n   601\t                    [(mw/gate\n   602\t                       {:dao.stream.middleware/verify\n   603\t                        (fn [d _ctx _req] (when (= :bad d) :no))\n   604\t                        :dao.stream.middleware/decision medium})])\n   605\t          op (fn [] (stream/next wrapped :my-c))]\n   606\t      (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome (op))))\n   607\t      (is (= [[:next :my-c]] @inner-calls)\n   608\t          \"a nil answer passes the request through unchanged\")\n   609\t      (is (= :dao.stream/refused (:dao.stream/outcome (op))))\n   610\t      (is (= [[:next :my-c]] @inner-calls)\n   611\t          \"a refusal is a short-circuit: the inner handle is not\n   612\t           consulted\")\n   613\t      (is (= [[:cursor :dao.stream/oldest] [:next :c0] [:next :c1]]\n   614\t             @calls)\n   615\t          \"one medium read per operation, the refusal consuming the last\"))))\n   616\t\n   617\t\n   618\t;; =============================================================================\n   619\t;; The exemplars\n   620\t;; =============================================================================\n   621\t\n   622\t(deftest metering-emits-per-operation-and-keeps-the-outcome\n   623\t  (let [target (ring 4)\n   624\t        meter (ring 8)\n   625\t        wrapped (mw/wrap target\n   626\t                         [(mw/metering {:meter/stream meter\n   627\t                                        :meter/identity \"peer-a\"})])\n   628\t        c (:dao.stream/cursor (stream/cursor wrapped :dao.stream/oldest))]\n   629\t    (is (= :dao.stream/blocked (:dao.stream/outcome (stream/next wrapped c))))\n   630\t    (is (= :dao.stream/ok\n   631\t           (:dao.stream/outcome (stream/append! wrapped :v))))\n   632\t    (is (= [{:meter/identity \"peer-a\"\n   633\t             :meter/op :dao.stream/cursor\n   634\t             :meter/outcome :dao.stream/ok}\n   635\t            {:meter/identity \"peer-a\"\n   636\t             :meter/op :dao.stream/next\n   637\t             :meter/outcome :dao.stream/blocked}\n   638\t            {:meter/identity \"peer-a\"\n   639\t             :meter/op :dao.stream/append!\n   640\t             :meter/outcome :dao.stream/ok}]\n   641\t           (drain-values meter))\n   642\t        \"one emission per operation, outcome returned unchanged\")))\n   643\t\n   644\t\n   645\t(deftest present-associates-the-credential-inward\n   646\t  (let [inner-calls (atom [])\n   647\t        log (atom [])\n   648\t        seen-reqs (atom [])\n   649\t        wrapped (mw/wrap\n   650\t                  (recording-handle inner-calls)\n   651\t                  [(mw/present\n   652\t                     {:dao.stream.middleware/present\n   653\t                      (fn [ctx _req]\n   654\t                        {:token (:dao.stream.remote/channel ctx)})})\n   655\t                   (spy :inside log\n   656\t                        (fn [_ctx req] (swap! seen-reqs conj req) req)\n   657\t                        pass-out)])\n   658\t        outcome (mw/apply-request wrapped\n   659\t                                  {:dao.stream.remote/channel \"a\"}\n   660\t                                  {:dao.stream.remote/op :dao.stream/append!\n   661\t                                   :dao.stream.remote/args [:v]})]\n   662\t    (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome outcome)))\n   663\t    (is (= [{:token \"a\"}]\n   664\t           (mapv :dao.stream.remote/credential @seen-reqs))\n   665\t        \"the credential rides the operation map inward\")\n   666\t    (is (= [[:append! :v]] @inner-calls)\n   667\t        \"the inner handle sees only the operation's own args\")\n   668\t    (is (= [[:in :inside] [:out :inside]] @log)\n   669\t        \"the out transform is identity\")))\n   670\t\n   671\t\n   672\t;; =============================================================================\n   673\t;; The index-interpreter exemplar publishing decisions\n   674\t;; =============================================================================\n   675\t\n   676\t(defn- index-fold\n   677\t  \"The slice's index-interpreter exemplar: folds the retained facts of\n   678\t   `facts` from `cursor`, deriving the running set of allowed channels\n   679\t   and appending each new state to `medium` as a decision. An\n   680\t   interpreter folds streams; only transforms are bound by the four\n   681\t   prohibitions. Returns the fold's final cursor.\"\n   682\t  [facts medium cursor]\n   683\t  (loop [cursor cursor, allowed #{}]\n   684\t    (let [r (stream/next facts cursor)]\n   685\t      (case (:dao.stream/outcome r)\n   686\t        :dao.stream/ok\n   687\t        (let [fact (:dao.stream/value r)\n   688\t              allowed (cond\n   689\t                        (contains? fact :middleware.test/allow)\n   690\t                        (conj allowed (:middleware.test/allow fact))\n   691\t                        (contains? fact :middleware.test/deny)\n   692\t                        (disj allowed (:middleware.test/deny fact))\n   693\t                        :else allowed)\n   694\t              appended (stream/append! medium allowed)]\n   695\t          (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome appended)))\n   696\t          (recur (:dao.stream/cursor r) allowed))\n   697\t        cursor))))\n   698\t\n   699\t\n   700\t(deftest the-index-interpreter-exemplar-publishes-decisions\n   701\t  (let [facts (ring 16)\n   702\t        medium (ring 1)\n   703\t        wrapped (mw/wrap\n   704\t                  (ring 4)\n   705\t                  [(mw/gate\n   706\t                     {:dao.str