{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,125p' src/cljc/dao/stream.cljc | nl -ba; sed -n '25,58p' docs/design/dao.shibi.md | nl -ba -v25\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns dao.stream\n     2\t  \"DaoStream v2: passive substrate for IO in datom.world.\n     3\t\n     4\t   Seven operations:\n     5\t     Five handle operations (protocols implemented per declared surface):\n     6\t       descriptor (universal reachability and identity projection)\n     7\t       cursor     (reader surface)\n     8\t       next       (reader surface)\n     9\t       append!    (writer surface)\n    10\t       close!     (closable surface)\n    11\t     Two transport entry functions (per-transport, host-composed):\n    12\t       create!    (creates a new logical stream from a creation specification)\n    13\t       attach!    (attaches to an existing stream via portable descriptor)\n    14\t\n    15\t   Result Convention:\n    16\t     Every operation returns an open outcome map keyed by :dao.stream/outcome.\n    17\t     All qualified keywords live under :dao.stream/…\n    18\t     Each operation has an exhaustive, closed outcome set.\"\n    19\t  (:refer-clojure :exclude [next]))\n    20\t\n    21\t\n    22\t;; =============================================================================\n    23\t;; The Seven Operations and Standard Keywords\n    24\t;; =============================================================================\n    25\t\n    26\t(def operations\n    27\t  \"The seven DaoStream v2 operations.\"\n    28\t  #{:create! :attach! :descriptor :cursor :next :append! :close!})\n    29\t\n    30\t\n    31\t(def surfaces\n    32\t  \"The public operational surfaces a handle may declare.\"\n    33\t  #{:reader :writer :closable})\n    34\t\n    35\t\n    36\t;; Anchors\n    37\t(def anchor-oldest\n    38\t  \"Earliest retained position on the stream.\"\n    39\t  :dao.stream/oldest)\n    40\t\n    41\t\n    42\t(def anchor-newest\n    43\t  \"Positioned after the newest appended value (observes next arrival).\"\n    44\t  :dao.stream/newest)\n    45\t\n    46\t\n    47\t(def standard-anchors\n    48\t  \"Contract-defined anchor keywords.\"\n    49\t  #{anchor-oldest anchor-newest})\n    50\t\n    51\t\n    52\t;; Closed outcome sets per operation (contract exhaustive tables)\n    53\t(def outcomes-create\n    54\t  #{:dao.stream/ok\n    55\t    :dao.stream/invalid-spec\n    56\t    :dao.stream/not-found\n    57\t    :dao.stream/transport-error})\n    58\t\n    59\t\n    60\t(def outcomes-attach\n    61\t  #{:dao.stream/ok\n    62\t    :dao.stream/invalid-descriptor\n    63\t    :dao.stream/not-found\n    64\t    :dao.stream/transport-error})\n    65\t\n    66\t\n    67\t(def outcomes-descriptor\n    68\t  #{:dao.stream/ok})\n    69\t\n    70\t\n    71\t(def outcomes-cursor\n    72\t  #{:dao.stream/ok\n    73\t    :dao.stream/invalid-anchor\n    74\t    :dao.stream/closed\n    75\t    :dao.stream/refused\n    76\t    :dao.stream/transport-error})\n    77\t\n    78\t\n    79\t(def outcomes-next\n    80\t  #{:dao.stream/ok\n    81\t    :dao.stream/blocked\n    82\t    :dao.stream/end\n    83\t    :dao.stream/gap\n    84\t    :dao.stream/cursor-mismatch\n    85\t    :dao.stream/invalid-cursor\n    86\t    :dao.stream/refused\n    87\t    :dao.stream/transport-error})\n    88\t\n    89\t\n    90\t(def outcomes-append\n    91\t  #{:dao.stream/ok\n    92\t    :dao.stream/full\n    93\t    :dao.stream/invalid-value\n    94\t    :dao.stream/closed\n    95\t    :dao.stream/refused\n    96\t    :dao.stream/transport-error})\n    97\t\n    98\t\n    99\t(def outcomes-close\n   100\t  #{:dao.stream/ok})\n   101\t\n   102\t\n   103\t(def operation-outcomes\n   104\t  \"Map of operation keyword to its closed outcome set.\"\n   105\t  {:create! outcomes-create\n   106\t   :attach! outcomes-attach\n   107\t   :descriptor outcomes-descriptor\n   108\t   :cursor outcomes-cursor\n   109\t   :next outcomes-next\n   110\t   :append! outcomes-append\n   111\t   :close! outcomes-close})\n   112\t\n   113\t\n   114\t(def outcome-required-keys\n   115\t  \"Map from [operation outcome] to required keys in the result map.\"\n   116\t  {[:create! :dao.stream/ok] #{:dao.stream/handle}\n   117\t   [:attach! :dao.stream/ok] #{:dao.stream/handle}\n   118\t   [:descriptor :dao.stream/ok] #{:dao.stream/descriptor :dao.stream/identity}\n   119\t   [:cursor :dao.stream/ok] #{:dao.stream/cursor}\n   120\t   [:next :dao.stream/ok] #{:dao.stream/value :dao.stream/cursor}\n   121\t   [:next :dao.stream/gap] #{:dao.stream/cursor}})\n   122\t\n   123\t\n   124\t;; =============================================================================\n   125\t;; Canonical Operation Resolution Helper\n    25\t\n    26\t- **Its index interpreter** observes ShiBi's fact streams (grants,\n    27\t  caveats, revocations, emitted decisions) with its own cursors,\n    28\t  materializes them as `dao.space.index` materializes covered indexes, and\n    29\t  publishes the resulting immutable query value, a relation value or an\n    30\t  opened published index, as the decision onto the gate's capacity-1\n    31\t  decision medium (`dao.stream.middleware.md`, gate). The value published\n    32\t  is the tuple space's state at that moment.\n    33\t- **Its query interpreter is `verify`**, and `verify` is the required\n    34\t  adapter contract: a pure function of one immutable query value, the\n    35\t  context and the request, evaluating ShiBi's authorization rules as a\n    36\t  Datalog query with the request as bindings, the shape\n    37\t  `dao.space.query/q` already has (a query over immutable inputs, opening\n    38\t  nothing), and answering nil or a reason.\n    39\t- **A `present`**, a pure function of context and request that produces\n    40\t  the value carried in `:dao.stream.remote/credential`.\n    41\t- **A reason vocabulary** under its own namespace for\n    42\t  `:dao.stream.middleware/reason`.\n    43\t- **Where use is metered**, the decision facts the gate emits, which the\n    44\t  index observes like any other fact stream.\n    45\t\n    46\t**Limits of the adapter contract**, stated precisely. `verify` runs\n    47\tsynchronously inside one operation on one snapshot: its cost per operation\n    48\tis bounded by the composition, and a query over an opened published index\n    49\tresolves only what is already local, because `verify` opens, fetches and\n    50\twaits for nothing; a rule that would need a remote read is a rule the index\n    51\tmust have materialized. Its input is the latest published snapshot, so a\n    52\tgrant or revocation is effective only once the index has observed and\n    53\tpublished it: staleness is bounded by the index's cadence and the medium's\n    54\teviction, and a policy that must fail closed does so on the `none` marker\n    55\tand the `ended` marker. A decision is per call and is not itself a fact\n    56\tunless the gate emits it.\n    57\t\n    58\t**Non-goal in this version.** Request-specific decisions published through\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
